            <ArticleTitle>Small-bowel perforation secondary to metastatic carcinoma of the breast.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>312</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Perforation from a solitary metastatic lesion of the small bowel is rare. We report a case of acute perforation with no evidence of metastatic disease within the abdomen. Resection of the small bowel was performed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
